{
  "question_index": 1031,
  "question": "Apple High School is holding graduation in their Fine Arts Center this year which has space for 6000 people.  After accounting for 950 seats for graduates and 300 seats for faculty attending, how many tickets would each graduate receive to give to their friends and family if the tickets are split equally?",
  "gt": "5",
  "full_completion": "To determine how many tickets each graduate would receive, I'll start by calculating the total number of seats available for graduates and faculty.\n\nFirst, I'll subtract the seats for graduates and faculty from the total capacity of the Fine Arts Center.\n\nTotal capacity: 6000\nSeats for graduates: 950\nSeats for faculty: 300\n\nTotal seats for graduates and faculty: 950 + 300 = 1250\n\nNow, I'll subtract this from the total capacity to find the remaining seats for graduates.\n\nRemaining seats for graduates: 6000 - 1250 = 4750\n\nSince the tickets are to be split equally among the graduates, I'll divide the remaining seats by the number of graduates.\n\nNumber of graduates: 4750 \u00f7 950 = 5\n\nEach graduate would receive 5 tickets.\n \nFinal Answer: 5\n```",
  "trimmed_completion": "To determine how many tickets each graduate would receive, I'll start by calculating the total number of seats available for graduates and faculty.\n\nFirst, I'll subtract the seats for graduates and faculty from the total capacity of the Fine Arts Center.\n\nTotal capacity: 6000\nSeats for graduates: 950\nSeats for faculty: 300\n\nTotal seats for graduates and faculty: 950 + 300 = 1250\n\nNow, I'll subtract this from the total capacity to find the remaining seats for graduates.\n\nRemaining seats for graduates: 6000 - 1250 = 4750\n\nSince the tickets are to be split equally among the graduates, I'll divide the remaining seats by the number of graduates.\n\nNumber of graduates: 4750 \u00f7 950 = 5\n\nEach graduate would receive 5 tickets.\n \nFinal Answer: 5\n```",
